{"id":"G4103","lemma":"πιστός","transliteration":"pistos","sayIt":"pistos","language":"Greek","partOfSpeech":"adjective","gloss":"faithful","meaning":"πιστός, -ή, -όν\n(πείθω), [in LXX chiefly for אָמַן ;]\nI. Pass., to be trusted or believed;\n1. of persons, trusty, faithful : Mat.24:45 25:21, 23 Luk.12:42, Act.16:15, 1Co.4:2 4:17 7:25, Eph.1:1 6:21, Col.1:2, 7 4:7, 9, 1Ti.1:12, 2Ti.2:2, Heb.2:17 3:2, 5, 1Pe.5:12, Rev.2:13 19:11; of God, 1Co.1:9 10:13, 2Co.1:18, 1Th.5:24, 2Th.3:3, Heb.10:23 11:11, 2Ti.2:13, 1Jn.1:9, 1Pe.4:19; before ἐν, Luk.16:10-12 19:17, 1Ti.3:11; ἐπί, with accusative, Mat.25:23; ἄχρι θανάτου, Rev.2:10; ὁ μάρτυς ὁ π., Rev.1:5; id. καὶ ἀληθινός, Rev.3:14.\n2. Of things, trustworthy, reliable, sure: Act.13:34, 1Ti.1:15 3:1 4:9, 2Ti.2:11, Tit.1:9 3:8, Rev.21:5 22:6.\nII. Act., believing, trusting, relying: Act.16:1, 2Co.6:15, Gal.3:9, 1Ti.4:10 5:16 6:2, Tit.1:6, Rev.17:14; pl., Act.10:45, 1Ti.4:3 4:12; opposite to ἄπιστος, Jhn.20:27; π. εἰς θεόν, 1Pe.1:21; π. ποιεῖν, III Jn 5.\n(On the difficulty of choosing in some cases between the active and the passive meaning, see Lft., Gal., 157.) †\n(AS)","glosses":["faithful","trustworthy","believe","believers","believing","sure blessings"],"count":63,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"mat-24","v":45,"renderings":{"bsb":"faithful","kjv":"a faithful"}},{"chapterId":"mat-25","v":21,"renderings":{"bsb":"faithful","kjv":"aithful"}},{"chapterId":"mat-25","v":23,"renderings":{"bsb":"faithful","kjv":"faithful"}},{"chapterId":"luk-12","v":42,"renderings":{"bsb":"faithful","kjv":"that faithful"}},{"chapterId":"luk-16","v":10,"renderings":{"bsb":"is faithful","kjv":"He that is faithful"}},{"chapterId":"luk-16","v":11,"renderings":{"bsb":"faithful","kjv":"faithful"}},{"chapterId":"luk-16","v":12,"renderings":{"bsb":"faithful","kjv":"faithful"}},{"chapterId":"luk-19","v":17,"renderings":{"bsb":"faithful","kjv":"faithful"}},{"chapterId":"jhn-20","v":27,"renderings":{"bsb":"believe"}},{"chapterId":"act-10","v":45,"renderings":{